
 Welcome to SAID64, the 64-bit version of SAID.
 Several new features have been added. The mail back
 option, "go9" has been improved, for example.

 Note! 
 SAID data file assignments can be changed at any time
 by entering "GO250"
 RETURN for non-graphics
 "TDL" to set PLOT time delay
 or enter TERMINAL type (XW, TK41, or ?) ->
 You are using the single meson photoproduction code
 from SAID64. This code contains the new, as of March 2011,
 Chew-Mandelstam parametrization form. It is
 unitary at the two-body level, and uses the hadronic
 amplitudes determined in fits to pi-N elastic and the
 pi-N -> eta-N reaction. The formalism is described in
 Phys. Rev. C 82, 035202 (2010).

 Access this solution after loading the default solution
 by using: go2, v, fa10
 (As always, case does not matter in SAID.)

 RETURN to continue ->
 New contour plotter- Enter CONP or "GO60" to view
 Note new "GO55" Chi2 summary option(alternate to "GO5")
 "GO56" Summarize fits compared to Single-Energy fits
 "GO29" to do your own resonance fit
 "GO28" get decay amplitudes(A1/2,A3/2) from GW solns
 "GO57" Compare MULTIPOLES for different solutions 6/05
 "GO58" another "Compare MULTIPOLES"
 "GO59" Print/Plot amplitudes (H, F, A) vs E, S, A, t..
 "GO7" then "Go27" to PLOT PiN amplitudes for any solution
 The experimental data file is
 PR094  Photo-prod          07/09 Arndt  08/18/14                

 CAUTION! do NOT use any solution outside its range of
 validity. Extrapolation properties are generally BAD!

 Eg(photon energy) thresholds are:  
 pion=  145. eta=   707. kaon=   912. MeV
 Kindly work ABOVE these energies to avoid nonsense.
 Enter "E" here to set up for eta photoproduction
 Enter "P" here to set up for etaprime photoproduction
 Enter "L" here to set up for k-Lambda photoproduction
 Enter "S" here to set up for k-Sigma photoproduction
 Enter "B" here to switch to "Benchmark" PR data

 RETURN to continue -> g2, w1, w2, r1, r2= 13.75 22.50  0.00  0.00  0.00   
  Solution:
  CM12 2700 MEV P(200) CHI/DP=51634/25553                SM05    8/ 5/26  
  "GO22" -punch params
 An "alternative" solution can be defined with a "GO51"
 RETURN to continue ->
  Enter first four letters of the desired solution
 "SES " will set up a "single-energy" soln with DIAGONAL ErrM
 "G2  " will allow change in BORN terms
 Enter OWN to input a solution -Return to see soln file -> g2, w1, w2, r1, r2= 13.75 16.00  0.00  0.00  0.00   
  Solution:
  SM95 2000 MEV P(135) CHI/DP=31810/13415      8/95       SM95   8/ 5/26  
  "GO22" -punch params
 An "alternative" solution can be defined with a "GO51"
 RETURN to continue ->

 CONTOUR(or 3-D) PLOT an observable over a specified
 kinematic range(Energy,Angle).
 Experimental data can be represented as DISTRIBUTION
 or as RESIDULES, (Obs(Sol)-Obs(Exp))/Err. A NORMALIZED
 CHi2 will be calculated for all displayed data.
 Graphic CURSOR can be used to MEASURE points (Energy, Angle)
 and Value) or to open a "window" by stroking "W" at E1,A1
 Stroke "E" at E2,A2 to PLOT (E1->E2,A1) with dA=A2-A1
 Stroke "A" at E2,A2 to PLOT (E1,A1->A2) dith dE=E2-E1
 Two solutions can be COMPARED by plots of DIFFERENCE
 Enter 0 to get a second solution; otherwise
 Enter 1(Soln1), 2(Soln2), 3(Soln1-Soln2) ->
 Enter an ENERGY range (Emin Emax) -> Reaction no-  1(PI0P) 2(PI+N) 3(PI-P) 4(PI0N)
 Enter reaction -> Type(DSG,P,...) ->
Thresholds=  144.76  151.65  148.43  144.74


 You are set to CONTOUR plot PI+N DSG 
 From  300.0 to  320.0 MeV  0<Acm<180 deg
 Max/Min=   0.000/  24.330
 "GO60" to re-enter CONPLOT
 "GO66" to specify different ENERGY range
 "GO61" to specify different REACTION
 "GO62" to specify different DATA type
 "GO63" to Renew PLOT
 "GO64" to READ a point from the PLOT, or draw a "window"
 Enter "D" to plot data distribution
 Enter "R" For RESIDUAL plot- R=(Obs1-Obs2)/Err Enter:
 R<1(red), R<2(yellow), R<3(green), R<4(lblue) ...
 Enter "3" to see a 3-dimensional plot
 RETURN to frame contour plot -> Set to display UN-flagged data ONLY
 Enter "F" to toggle flag/UNflag data
 Enter "S" to use selective data sets
